/lgtm

I was surprised to find out that kubelet apparently does all probes in a loop, not in parallel with each other (?)

```
probeLoop:
	for w.doProbe(ctx) {
		// Wait for next probe tick.
		select {
		case <-w.stopCh:
			break probeLoop
		case <-probeTicker.C:
		case <-w.manualTriggerCh:
			// continue
		}
	}
```

so I guess now we'll block for max 1 second in each Close() but before we could potentially block for CLOSE_WAIT time? (Unless I didn't read deeply enough and the socket is actually nonblocking...)

So yeah, 1 is better than 60. Only downside I can think of is that if the app is overloaded, and doesn't get around to answering the probe within 1s, then perhaps we'd get a failure when the app might have been able to finish sending or close in 5 seconds or something. But if not 1s then where...

